/// The parts of a replica of the sculpt as sweeps (engine/sweep.wrela): a leg is one sweep from
/// its hip or elbow through its joints to its toes, the tail one from its root to its tip; the
/// torso, neck, head and the small parts are straight sweeps. Each part's control sections
/// (`sections`, evenly along its path, 4 bumps each) are fitted to radii measured in its own
/// planes.
///
/// Radii measured every centimetre along each path; each path runs on 2 cm past its ends. Parts
/// join with 8 mm smooth seams: where several fitted parts overlap (the hindquarters), their
/// surfaces cross, and a hard union shows the plates.
